I agree that this is a suicidal mission.  The challenge is that you
have to code for many months or years without much of an effect
(you're making something that's already there).  I was trying to get
some ideas for how to have new versions of Nethack, as I think the
game will die natural death if no one releases anything.  Of course we
could continue with the current code, for example concentrate on
Sporkhack.   Do you see Spork as an ongoing project or is it just some
YANIs that you decided to add for fun?

I'm wondering whether the death (or deep sleep?) of vanilla Nethack
and Slashem is because of the poor design and code and that authors
get discouraged by it.  If that's the case, then the only hope is a
rewrite.  On the other hand, the Linux kernel is an excellent piece of
code, and it would be insane to rewrite it just because it's C.


